 ## [0.1.2] - 2026-10-02
 
-Agent compatibility, constrained decoding that says what it cannot do, a bounded SSD prefix cache,
-and sampled requests that use speculative decoding.
+Use Yunshu with Claude Code, Codex and opencode, get clearer model capability
+errors, and reuse prompts across restarts with a bounded local disk cache.
+Sampled requests can now use speculative decoding. This is an editorial summary
+of the published release; later main improvements are listed under Unreleased.
+
+### Highlights
+
+- Coding agents can use native tools and model aliases; `yunshu launch` supplies
+  the served model's context and effort settings. [Compatibility evidence](docs/guides/AGENT_COMPAT.md).
+- Sampled 27B agent requests decoded at **69–93 tok/s**, up from **20 tok/s** in
+  the recorded comparison. [Performance evidence](docs/reports/PERF_TREND.md).
+- Reuse exact prompt checkpoints after restart, with a **64 GiB** default disk
+  budget and free-space reserve. Inspect or clean them with `yunshu cache`.
+- Diagnose problems locally: `yunshu doctor`, `yunshu diagnose`, cache checks and
+  rotated logs provide fixes while redacting secrets.
+
+### Upgrade notes / breaking changes
+
+- Unsupported regex and schema constructs now return HTTP 400 instead of being
+  ignored or approximated. Requests exceeding supported context or model
+  capabilities also return explicit errors.
+- The disk prompt cache is on at `~/.yunshu/cache/apc`; set
+  `YUNSHU_VLM_APC_DISK=0` to opt out. Reserve: larger of 10% free space or 20 GiB.
+- Experimental tool-call grammar remains off. Removed `YUNSHU_LANE_LINEAR` no
+  longer controls decoding; the measured implementation is the default.
+- Mid-conversation instructions and tools use the model's native template;
+  client-visible tool parsing and error behavior changed to preserve structure.
+
