+## [0.1.1] - 2026-09-29
+
+Yunshu focuses on local LLM/VLM inference on Apple Silicon, with Qwen3.8-27B as
+the first tuned model. This release improves prompt reuse, decoding, tools and
+first-run setup while keeping other modalities available as supported capabilities.
+
+### Highlights
+
+- Repeated 8K prompts start in **0.1 s**, down from **9 s** in the historical
+  Qwen3.8-27B test. [Sources](docs/BENCHMARKS.md).
+- Decode the recorded 27B server workload at **80 tok/s**, up from **57 tok/s**,
+  with verified speculative output. [Sources](docs/reports/PERF_TREND.md).
+- Long-context decode improves **24.5 → 46.6 tok/s** at 131K in the recorded
+  comparison; short-context differences were within noise. [Sources](docs/reports/PERF_TREND.md).
+- `yunshu doctor`, `yunshu pull` and `yunshu config` make setup and configuration
+  errors actionable; interrupted downloads resume instead of duplicating models.
+
+### Upgrade notes / breaking changes
+
+- `yunshu serve` now binds `127.0.0.1` by default. Set the host explicitly for
+  network access and protect it with `--auth-token`.
+- Models default to `~/.yunshu/models`; `YUNSHU_MODELS_DIR` overrides it. Rate
+  limiting is off by default (`YUNSHU_RATE_LIMIT_RPM=0`).
+- Lossy cache precision remains opt-in: native disk precision is the default,
+  text cache quantization is off, and `YUNSHU_KV_PRECISION=int8` trades accuracy
+  for memory. Existing int8 disk entries still load.
+- Removed settings: `YUNSHU_PACKED_5BIT`, `YUNSHU_VLM_KV_BITS`,
+  `YUNSHU_VLM_INVARIANT`, `YUNSHU_MTP_FAST_VERIFY`, `YUNSHU_RAGGED_KV`.
+  Measured decoding/cache implementations replace those switches.
+- The deprecated Python `Engine` class and distributed/multi-tenant leftovers
+  were removed. Depend on the documented CLI/API, not deleted internals.
+- Updated dependencies include MLX 0.32.2, transformers 5.17 and mlx-vlm 0.7.3.
+  `reasoning_effort` is passed to supporting templates rather than a token cap.
 
 ### Performance
 
-- Sampled requests use speculative decoding (position-keyed Gumbel sampling makes draft acceptance
-  exact): sampled 27B agent traffic 20 to 69-93 tok/s, token distribution checked against the
-  serial sampler.
-- The APC SSD tier reloads bit-exact checkpoints 10-40x faster than re-prefill on 27B and survives
-  restarts; a longer SSD prefix beats a short RAM hit on the text engine.
-- Byte-bounded prefix cache with superseded checkpoints dropped and an end-of-system-turn checkpoint.
-- Ported oMLX SiLU probe and `qmv_fast` layout rule (27B greedy output identical, decode unchanged).
